  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7e4be555-759b-40ed-9407-01ec246c885e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1152,
        832
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## EmailAutoReply\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors Gmail for incoming messages and filters them through an If condition. Messages that match the criteria are mapped into fields such as candidate email, subject, and company email, then passed to an AI agent to generate a structured reply. The generated response is sent by the email node, while messages that do not match the condition are ignored.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect and authorize the Gmail Trigger credentials for the inbox that should be monitored.\n- Configure the If node with the exact criteria that determine which emails should receive an auto-reply.\n- Review the Edit Fields node mappings for candidateEmail, subject, and companyEmail so they match the incoming Gmail payload.\n- Add OpenAI credentials for the chat model used by the AI Agent and verify the structured output parser matches the expected reply format.\n- Configure the Send an Email node with valid email-sending credentials and the desired sender, recipient, subject, and body fields.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the If conditions, field mappings, AI prompt, structured output schema, and email template to fit different auto-reply scenarios or tone of voice."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "00e89f2c-a1dd-4ded-a0c9-dfb41a0ff7c0",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -592,
        1024
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Receive and filter email\n\nStarts when a new Gmail message arrives and evaluates it with a conditional branch to decide whether it should receive an automated response."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "17de9042-330c-4a19-864b-d2ba1361957e",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        832
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## Prepare or ignore message\n\nHandles the two nearby branch outcomes: eligible emails have key fields extracted and normalized, while non-eligible emails are routed to a no-op path."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
